.TH HOTLAB-GATEWAY 1 "@DATE@" "hotlab @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hotlab-gateway \- RDP gateway that starts Proxmox lab VMs on demand
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hotlab-gateway
.br
.B hotlab-gateway mint-rdp
.I user
.B \-\-address
.I host[:port]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B hotlab-gateway deploy
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B hotlab-gateway teardown
.B \-\-out
.I dir
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without a verb,
.B hotlab-gateway
runs the RDP listener (normally as
.BR hotlab-gateway.service ).
It reads the routing token or user name from each client's first RDP packet,
starts the user's Proxmox VE virtual machine if needed, and relays the
connection to it.
.PP
.B mint-rdp
writes an .rdp file carrying a signed routing token.
.B deploy
creates one clone of a source VM per user, with guest accounts and .rdp files;
.B teardown
removes a deployment again. Run a verb without arguments for its options.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read, later sources winning, from
.IR /usr/lib/hotlab-gateway/appsettings.json ,
.I $HOTLAB_CONFIG_DIR/appsettings.json
(default
.IR /etc/hotlab/appsettings.json ),
systemd credentials in
.I $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY
(a file named
.B Hotlab__Proxmox__TokenSecret
supplies
.BR Hotlab:Proxmox:TokenSecret ;
see
.BR SECRETS ),
environment variables such as
.BR Hotlab__Tokens__SigningKey ,
and the command line.
The user map is reloaded from
.B $HOTLAB_USERS_FILE
.RI ( /etc/hotlab/users.json
for the service) when it changes.
.SH SECRETS
Encrypt the Proxmox token secret and the routing-token signing key, for example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
install \-d \-m 0700 /etc/credstore.encrypted
systemd-creds encrypt \-\-name=Hotlab__Proxmox__TokenSecret \- \e
    /etc/credstore.encrypted/Hotlab__Proxmox__TokenSecret
systemd-creds encrypt \-\-name=Hotlab__Tokens__SigningKey \- \e
    /etc/credstore.encrypted/Hotlab__Tokens__SigningKey
.fi
.RE
.PP
then load them into the service with a drop-in: run
.B systemctl edit hotlab-gateway
and add
.PP
.RS
.nf
[Service]
LoadCredentialEncrypted=Hotlab__Proxmox__TokenSecret:/etc/credstore.encrypted/Hotlab__Proxmox__TokenSecret
LoadCredentialEncrypted=Hotlab__Tokens__SigningKey:/etc/credstore.encrypted/Hotlab__Tokens__SigningKey
.fi
.RE
.PP
followed by
.BR "systemctl restart hotlab-gateway" .
systemd decrypts each credential into the service's
.IR $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hotlab/appsettings.json
Site settings.
.TP
.I /etc/hotlab/users.json
User-to-VM map, maintained by
.BR "deploy \-\-users\-file\-target" .
.TP
.I /etc/credstore.encrypted/
Suggested location for the secrets, encrypted with
.BR systemd-creds (1).
They are not loaded automatically: the packaged unit only documents the
.B LoadCredentialEncrypted=
lines, commented out (see
.BR SECRETS ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd-creds (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.I /usr/share/doc/hotlab-gateway/README.md.gz
